---
// Primer · For newcomers. Sets up *why* AI agents are needed for
// specialized scientific work before the rest of the landing page
// dives into AKD specifics. Sourced verbatim-ish from front.md and
// tightened for the page voice.
---
<section class="section section--primer" id="primer">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Primer · For newcomers</span>
      <h2>Why AI agents — and what makes one well-designed?</h2>
      <p>Three foundations that everything else on this page builds on.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="primer-rows">
      <article class="primer-row">
        <div class="primer-row__lead">
          <span class="primer-row__num">01</span>
          <h3>The jagged edge of AI</h3>
          <p class="primer-row__hint">Why generic chatbots fall short in science</p>
        </div>
        <div class="primer-row__body">
          <p>Standard AI chatbots often lack access to the specialized tools, databases, terminology, and ontologies needed for advanced scientific work — so they carry a higher risk of hallucinating in narrow technical domains.</p>
          <p>The value a chatbot provides usually depends on the user&rsquo;s own domain expertise. A subject-matter expert can ask precise questions, recognize weak reasoning, and quickly judge whether an answer is correct. A novice may not be sure what to ask, which assumptions to challenge, or how to verify a response. AI performs well on some tasks and fails unexpectedly on others that look similar.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="primer-row">
        <div class="primer-row__lead">
          <span class="primer-row__num">02</span>
          <h3>An agent is a digital worker</h3>
          <p class="primer-row__hint">From responding to acting</p>
        </div>
        <div class="primer-row__body">
          <p>An AI agent can be viewed as an independent digital worker. You give it a task, and it determines how to accomplish it.</p>
          <p>Unlike a chatbot, which mainly responds to questions, an agent takes action — analyzes a problem, breaks it into smaller steps, uses the right tools, reviews intermediate results, and corrects mistakes as it works toward completion.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="primer-row">
        <div class="primer-row__lead">
          <span class="primer-row__num">03</span>
          <h3>What makes an agent well-designed</h3>
          <p class="primer-row__hint">Reasoning · Context · Tools</p>
        </div>
        <div class="primer-row__body">
          <ul class="primer-elements" aria-label="Three core elements of a well-designed agent">
            <li>
              <b>Reasoning logic</b>
              <span>Often expressed as prompts or instructions that shape how the agent thinks through a task.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Contextual information</b>
              <span>Grounds the agent&rsquo;s reasoning in the specific scientific domain it serves.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Tool access</b>
              <span>With clear guidance on which tool to use, when to use it, and how to use it correctly.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>Designed this way, an agent can capture an expert&rsquo;s implicit knowledge — how to reason through a task, what context matters, which tools to reach for. A novice using the agent can then approach the productivity of an expert because that judgment is embedded in the workflow.</p>
          <p class="primer-row__caveat">Designing an agent for complex scientific tasks is not a purely technical exercise. It requires close collaboration among developers, scientists, domain experts, and end users — which is exactly the process AKD encodes.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .section--primer {
    /* Tighten the top spacing so the primer sits close to the
       OpenProjectBanner without losing breathing room. */
    padding-top: 80px;
  }

  .primer-rows {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 56px;
    margin-top: 12px;
  }

  .primer-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(220px, 280px) 1fr;
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  /* Separator between rows — subtle dashed line, accent dot at left. */
  .primer-row + .primer-row {
    padding-top: 56px;
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--border);
  }

  .primer-row__lead {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    position: sticky;
    top: 92px; /* below sticky nav (68px) + a little air */
    align-self: start;
  }
  .primer-row__num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 44px;
    line-height: 1;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .primer-row__lead h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 24px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    color: var(--text);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .primer-row__hint {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .primer-row__body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    max-width: 640px;
  }
  .primer-row__body p {
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .primer-row__body em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .primer-row__caveat {
    padding-left: 14px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    font-size: 15.5px !important;
  }

  /* Three-element list inside row 03 — small bordered cards. */
  .primer-elements {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 4px 0 6px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .primer-elements li {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: 12px 14px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .primer-elements b {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 14.5px;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .primer-elements span {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  /* ── Responsive ───────────────────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .primer-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 20px;
    }
    .primer-row__lead {
      position: static;
      top: auto;
    }
    .primer-row__num { font-size: 36px; }
    .primer-elements { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
